ukemoid reaction", "Metastatic cancer syndrome: Unlikely without focal symptoms or imaging evidence", "Diabetic ketoacidosis: Glucose is normal (99 mg/dL) and no metabolic acidosis (HCO3- 22 mEq/L)"], "alarm_features": ["Constitutional B symptoms (fever, night sweats, weight loss)", "Pancytopenia with blasts", "Acute neurological symptoms in a systemically unwell patient"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.6738025307510545, "posterior": 0.08162027582041659, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": ["Peripheral blasts with pancytopenia are pathognomonic for acute leukemia, strongly favoring acute myelogenous leukemia (B2) over myeloid neoplasm (B1) due to b…"], "evidence_against": ["Lack of fibrosis or cytogenetic markers reduces support for chronic myeloid disorders like primary myelofibrosis or blast crisis CML. This weakly argues agains…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["acute myeloid leukemia", "myelodysplastic syndrome with excess blasts", "chronic myeloid leukemia in blast crisis"]}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.344, "danger": 0.75, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.590700218625091, "posterior": 0.5150263220621247, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Lack of fibrosis or cytogenetic markers reduces support for chronic myeloid disorders like primary myelofibrosis or blast crisis CML. This weakly argues agains…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.7, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": ["chronic myeloid leukemia", "polycythemia vera", "essential thrombocythemia", "primary myelofibrosis"]}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.059, "danger": 0.5, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Peripheral blasts with pancytopenia are pathognomonic for acute leukemia, strongly favoring acute myelogenous leukemia (B2) over myeloid neoplasm (B1) due to b…"]}, "kb_reactive_non_malignant_l": {"id": "kb_reactive_non_malignant_l", "label": "reactive / non-malignant leukocytosis", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 1.0898649527956053e-07, "danger": 0.0, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Peripheral blasts with pancytopenia are pathognomonic for acute leukemia, strongly favoring acute myelogenous leukemia (B2) over myeloid neoplasm (B1) due to b…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 0.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.0, "interrupt_relevance": 0.0, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B3"], "other_mass": 0.0, "actions_taken": [{"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the normal serum creatinine (1.1 mg/dL) and absence of monoclonal protein detection in labs argue against plasma cell disorder?", "summary": "Normal renal function and no monoclonal protein in labs strongly argue against plasma cell disorder (B4), with weak exclusion."}, {"t": 4, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "cont